# Tailwind values

Do not use arbitrary Tailwind values. A class name has no square brackets.

Add a design value to `@theme` in `src/theme.css`, then use the utility it generates. Add a one-off property as a named `@utility` in that file.

```tsx
// Bad
className="size-[48px] gap-[8px] [image-rendering:pixelated]"

// Good
className="pixelated size-swatch gap-choice"
```

A length that changes with data stays a CSS variable on the element. A named utility reads it. The calculation does not go in a class name.
